Thanks, added `TestResponseWriterWrapper_StreamWrite_FallbackReasoningModeration` in `aigateway/handler/response_writer_wrapper_test.go`. It drives the real stream writer with the actual moderation component (`NewModerationImplWithClient`); only the moderation service client is stubbed, and it flags text only when it contains the fallback marker. Cases:

- primary (`reasoning_content`) and fallback (`reasoning`) differ and only the fallback is sensitive: the original chunk is not forwarded (only the sensitive-stop chunk and `[DONE]` are written);
- empty primary, sensitive fallback only: blocked the same way;
- moderation disabled: the event passes through byte-for-byte.

The first case fails if the fallback-field moderation in `chatCompletionChunkModerationText` is reverted.

This comment was drafted with the help of an AI assistant (Claude Code) and the change was tested locally.
